      "text": "Thirty-six percent of the Reproducibility Project: Psychology replications produced statistically significant results in the same direction as the original studies.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "pos": 4,
      "text": "Gilbert and colleagues argued that many Reproducibility Project replications used protocols that departed from the original studies.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "pos": 5,
      "text": "Obtaining the original author's endorsement of the replication protocol before data collection is a standard safeguard in replication research.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
